title: TeaParty
position: -263,-232
---
<<set $name1 to "Protagonist">>
<<set $name2 to "Ghost Child">>
<<set $mean to 0>>
// You walk into the first room. The interior is really high-class and luxurious, though the room itself isn't that big. There's a little girl standing/sitting by an assortment of chairs around a small table with small cups and a teapot. The other chairs are taken by plushies, only one is empty.
//there's a sign, not unlike the one in the hallway, next to the entrance. It reads "Task 1: Attend the party."
// You interact with the girl in order to trigger the following dialogue sequence:

{$name2}: Wah, hello. It's so good you're finally here! We were just about to start.
{$name1}: Oh, uhm- start with what?
{$name2}: Well, with the tea party of course! You came just at the right time. There's a spare seat left just for you.

-> What kind of tea party is this? There's just water in these cups.
    {$name2}: Ah ... I'm sorry. This is all I have for now. My mom will notice if I sneak up tea bags.
    <<set $mean = $mean + 1>>
-> Thank you! That's so thoughtful of you.
    {$name2}: Hee-hee, of course! You are my esteemed guest, after all.
{$name2}: Well then, sit down M'lady!

// You go to the empty chair and sit down. Before you have the option to explore the room a little, but there's nothing relevant to your objective - except that you can take note of the closet, which will say something like "it's stuffed pretty full but there's still enough room for one person to squeeze in."
The chair is sized for a small child, but it holds your weight, fortunately.
The little girl diligently serves you your "tea". The cup is small enough to hold between two fingers.
Actually, you're really thirsty. Like, incredibly so.
But the little girl is only halfway through serving all her "guests" when the teapot doesn't shed another drop.
{$name2}: Aw, it's empty. Just wait a moment. I'll go refill it.
She hurries off through a door you hadn't noticed before.
Your throat's dry as a desert.
-> Just drink up right now.
    {$name1}: It's not like she'll notice, right?
    <<set $cup to "empty">>
    <<set $mean = $mean + 1>>
-> Wait till she comes back.
    {$name1}: This ghost girl looks rich and cultured. I should probably be on my best behavior for this one.
    <<set $cup to "full">>

You're starting to get anxious as the moments tick by. Did you already fail? Were you not supposed to let her leave?
But finally, the girl returns. She proudly holds the teapot in her little hands.
{$name2}: Sorry it took a while. I had to sneak past my mom. She can't find out you're up here. Or else she'll get really mad.
She sits down in her spot next to you. You notice her glance at your tiny cup.
<<if $cup is "empty">>
    Her expression drops slightly.
    {$name2}: You know ... you're supposed to wait until everyone's at the table. It's rude if you don't.
    {$name1}: Ah! I'm sorry.
    {$name2}: It's okay. You can have a refill.
<<else>>
    A little smile appears on her face.
    {$name2}: Yay! Drink up, everyone!
<<endif>>
{$name2}: The party is on! If you want more, just serve yourself - there's enough tea for everyone.
Awesome. Who knows when you'll next get some fresh water?
You drink in silence. The little girl keeps glancing around as if expecting the plushies to say something.
{$name1}: (thinking) This is so awkward ... I should try and initiate some conversation.
{$name1}: So ... what's your name?
{$name2}: I'm Elizabeth. But feel free to call me Ellie!
<<set $name2 to "Ellie">>
{$name2}: Oh, I should introduce the rest too! The purple gentleman is Sir Thomas the great knight. And this here is Miss Anne.
{$name1}: Nice to meet you. I'm (insert name). So ... are they your usual guests?
{$name2}: Yes. Originally your seat belonged to Sir Arthur, but he was tragically slain in battle. He fought valiently.
-> Do you not have any normal friends?
    <<set $mean = $mean + 1>>
    You can see Ellie's bottom lip jut out and tremble a little.
    {$name2}: They are perfectly normal friends. The best. Also, it's rude to say that when they can hear you.
    {$name1}: Woah. She's pretty sensitive. Better be careful what I say.
-> Well, it's an honor to be a part of this fine gathering.
    {$name2}: *blushes* It's fine. You're a guest of honor.
// more dialogue but I don't have time right now ahhhhhh

<<if $mean < 3>>
{$name2}: If you're really hungry, I can go and try to sneak some cookies from the kitchen.
{$name1}: Woah. You would do that?
{$name2}: Of course. Just for you, though!
//here the screen maybe fades out so we just get the text until she gets back?
She leaves the room once again. This time, she's gone longer than when she fetched the water earlier.
But eventually she returns and proudly pulls from behind her back a pack of cookies.
<<declare $cookies = 5>>
<<else>>
{$name2}: Ah, sorry ... unfortunately I can't have any food in here. And if my mom catches me trying to sneak some up, she's gonna get real mad at me.
<<endif>>

// Idea: in every/most rooms you can find bonus items which are not exactly essential to winning the game, but they can be used to bring down your insanity counter or maybe replenish some health, depending on what variables we decide to include in the whole thing.

//a very short while later this next part happens

Suddenly you hear something. Clearly, you're not just imagining things. Ellie looks to be listening as well.
The sound of steps grows louder from outside that door.
{$name2}: Oh no. I think mom's coming this way! Quick, you have to hide somewhere. There - go into the closet. Also, Mom has really good ears so hold your breath whenever she gets near. 

//a countdown appears. You have to hide in the closet. Once you're in, text appears like in the hallway that says:
Press F to hold your breath.
//you get the initial 30 seconds of holding your breath. Starting at like 10, it will get tougher and you'll hear a heartbeat speeding up, while the screen gets a bit shaky and/or darker. Once the countdown runs out, you gasp, which instantly alerts the momster. If she's in your immediate vicinity, you are dead. If not, she just comes over fast and stands in front of the door for 5 seconds (which basically means you're done as well cause of the next part). In addition, every second of breath you held will take like 2 seconds to recover. So you need to time it well. There's two steps: one auditory, where you hear her steps and wheezing grow louder. Ideally, you start holding your breath in that moment. Otherwise, she will get alerted and stand in front of the closet (visual cue - she's looking in through the crack between the closet doors) for a little longer than normally. Not pressing F while she's in your field of view is instant death.

//after the momster leaves
{$name2}: (with a hint of sadness on her face) You should probably leave now. It's almost dinner time.
{$name1}: Hey, thanks for having me. It was nice. Um ... keep your chin up, alright?

//cue the sound of a door unlocking. You can now leave the way you came.


//we'll have to see how exactly this works chronologically, but if the mean counter exceeds a certain value (like 5 for example) Ellie will get out and run out of the room crying (or maybe she stays in the room but just starts crying which summons the momster). You then get the above mom sequence except it'll be less time for the countdown and Ellie won't tell you where to hide, or about holding your breath. Afterwards you'll apologize to Ellie. Maybe she'll say she wouldn't knowingly "feed" anyone to the momster and send you on your way. You did attend the party after all, even if not exactly nicely.

<<jump Kagome>>
