title: Cafeteria
position: -297,175
---
When you walk up to the door this time, you can hear the hustle of bustle of voices and the clattering of plates and all other sorts of things.
This is the final door.
Are you going in?
-> Go in.
//this option might appear twice just for show
//insert the sound effect of a door sliding open as the screen briefly fades to black.
{$name1}: Woah ... so many people. It looks ... just like a regular school cafeteria.
You look around and take in the unusual sight. It's almost like you're no longer at the spirit hotel at all.
Everyone's wearing the same uniform. Everyone is - even ...
{$name1}: Wait, why am I wearing the school uniform? I don't like this.
There's no sign this time. No instructions what to do.
You better figure out the task yourself.
//you then go exploring and can interact with multiple things. Of course, the important aspect is the interaction that appears when you spot the Drowned Child, which is this:
I look around. This kid is the only one sitting at a table all by themselves.
Although they are wearing the boy's uniform, you're not certain whether they are actually a boy or a girl.
Their chin-long hair hangs into their face. It looks deliberate. Like they're trying not to look at anyone, or to not have people look at them.
The tray of food in front of them is untouched, and their uniform is a bit sloppy, dirty here and there.
?: Hey! Are you new?
You turn to the sound of the voice. There are three teenage girls standing behind you, all smiling at you.
?: Is this your first day? Hey, why don't you come sit with us?
-> Sure, why not?
    <<jump DrownedChildBadEnding>>
-> No, thank you.
    Their expressions shift like day and night. Their faces turn to grotesque grimaces.
    ?: Really? But there's no other free seats. Where are you going to sit, then?
    You turn back. There are freee seats, of course - an entirely free table. Except now the kid is staring back at you with the same freakish grimace.
    And you think now, maybe there's actually a reason the table is empty.
    Are you really sure you want to sit there?
    -> ... nevermind, the girls seemed nice after all.
        <<jump DrownedChildBadEnding>>
    -> Yeah, I'm placing my bets on the quiet kid.
        <<jump DrownedChildGoodEnding>>
