title: DrownedChildBadEnding
position: -53,321
---
    They smile at each other, and then you.
    ?: Yay! Welcome to the gang!
    Before you follow them, you turn around once more and shudder.
    The lonely child is staring at you through their strands of hair.
    Their face is pure, unbridled hatred.
    And suddenly, you find yourself locked in that stare.
    You can't move. Can't even blink.
    The sounds around you begin to fade, like someone is turning down the volume.
    The room starts dissolving, until there's only you in a black void, and that table in front of you, with the middle schooler's jet black eyes still locked onto yours.
    And then, laughter swells from behind you.

===

title: DrownedChildGoodEnding

position: 374,237
---
//The question how the "mean" counters of the individual rooms are added up: You could just take the total sum of "mean" responses and make a cutoff value for each of the three different responses. In that case, there's no need for the separate variables. 
//Orrrr you could also go something along the lines of: If your total sum is below the cutoff value but you were overwhelmingly mean to one of the children, that also counts as being "too mean". Annyway:
<<set $dc to "The Drowned Child">>

<<if $mean + $mean2 + $mean3 + $mean4 < 4>>
The child smiles at you.
{$dc}: Nice to see you love children just as much as I do.
{$dc}: It was heartwarming, watching you interact with them. You were so gentle with them - thank you.
{$dc}: And ... good luck.
{$dc}: This trial can be harsh. If you ever find yourself in a pickle ... I'll help out if I can.
<<set $ally to true>>

<<elseif $mean + $mean2 + $mean3 + $mean4 < 10>>
You get a slight frown from the child.
{$dc}: Though ... I'd ask you to work on your empathy. And I hope you're not looking to go into child care.
{$dc}: I know you were probably just trying to be funny, but these kids have been through enough.
{$dc}: Still ... I can tell your heart is in the right place.
The child flashes a tentative smile.
{$dc}: So ... thank you. And good luck.
<<set $ally to true>>

<<elseif $mean + $mean2 + $mean3 + $mean4 >= 10>>
The child looks different somehow. They have changed their uniform to the female one. And they are dripping wet, algae stuck to their hair and clothes.
But most importantly, their shy, dead-eyed stare from the cafeteria has changed entirely.
They are glaring you with seething hatred.
This can't be good. Did you fail?
But you passed all the rooms, didn't you?
The child starts speaking in a messed-up, distorted kind of voice.
{$dc}: Well. Looks like you made the right call in the end.
{$dc}: Kind of surprising with how you've behaved up until now.
{$dc}: It says a lot about a person how they behave towards the most vulnerable of us. And you ...
{$dc}: Well. I hardly think it was your altruistic heart that got you here. That made you choose to help me in the end.
{$dc}: You pass anyway. Now get out, and never show your face around here again.
<<set $ally to true>>

<<endif>>

===